{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"aae3b4e2-34e0-44e5-bcd4-51ab1c0ba9bb","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have investigated the issue, fixed the bug preventing notifications, and documented the causes in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-W494dC/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Causes\n\n1. **Fatal Zsh Error (`status` is read-only)**:\n   In [bin/nightly-review.zsh](file:///tmp/h-W494dC/bin/nightly-review.zsh), line 19 assigned the exit code using `status=$?`. In `zsh`, `status` is a built-in read-only variable (an alias for `$?`). Assigning to it causes the fatal error:\n   ```\n   /Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status\n   ```\n   Because zsh terminates immediately upon this error, execution never reached lines 21–24 where `\"$NOTIFY\"` would have reported the failure.\n\n2. **Claude CLI Authentication Failure**:\n   The job was failing at line 18 because the `claude` command was not authenticated, logging `Not logged in · Please run /login` in [nightly-review.err](file:///tmp/h-W494dC/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err).\n\n### Changes Made\n\n- Modified [bin/nightly-review.zsh](file:///tmp/h-W494dC/bin/nightly-review.zsh) to use `exit_code=$?` instead of `status=$?`, allowing the error handling block to execute and notify on failures.\n- Documented the findings and remediation steps in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-W494dC/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":69.761422,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":155686,"output_tokens":2065,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":243362,"total_tokens":157751}}}
